{
 "points": [
  {
   "id": "P1.1",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Limited novelty: objective is SOMBRL/MaxInfoRL in continuous time; theory reuses OCORL components.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.2",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Regret bound requires exponentially large lambda, but experiments hand-tune or auto-tune lambda.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.3",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Main-text Theorem 1 hides lambda factor containing beta_N and e^{LT}; constants undiscussed.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.4",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Bounds for Theorems 1 and 2 differ between main text and appendix.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.5",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Theorem 1 proof is GP-specific (RKHS); calibration assumption for BNN ensembles unverified.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.6",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Practical algorithm uses mean model outside confidence set, so theory does not cover it.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.7",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Theorem 2 statement for lambda to infinity inconsistent with proof whose bound diverges.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.8",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Proof gaps: missing 1/N, unexplained Cauchy-Schwarz step, assumed variance monotonicity.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.9",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Theorem 2 bounds uncertainty only; no dynamics-error or downstream-task guarantee.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.10",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Inconsistent Lipschitz constants and sigma indices across equations and lemmas.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.11",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Scalability claim weak: OCORL comparison only on two small GP tasks.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.12",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Missing baselines: SOMBRL/MaxInfoRL, modern MBRL, intrinsic-motivation methods, discrete-time COMBRL.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.13",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Experiments use fixed-rate equidistant control; continuous time barely exercised.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.14",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Adaptive-sampling experiment only two tasks with final returns; sample-efficiency claim unverifiable.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.15",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Few seeds, standard-error bands only, no significance analysis; overlapping curves.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.16",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Lambda tuning budgets for COMBRL and baselines undescribed; possible unfair tuning.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.17",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Model quality never measured directly; globally accurate model claim untested.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.18",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Inflated claims (state of the art, largest gains in sparse tasks) without analysis.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.19",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Strong assumptions (noise-free derivatives, deterministic systems); no noisy or hardware experiments.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.1",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Primary-task gains modest; error bars overlap Mean Planning in 5 of 7 tasks.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.2",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Assumes familiarity with SAC, iCEM, TaCoS without introduction.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.3",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Novelty unclear: reward plus epistemic uncertainty objective not new; integration of existing components.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.4",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Algorithm 1 lacks detail on optimistic objective solving, rollouts and model updates.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.1",
   "reviewer": "Q2",
   "text": "Evaluation should report coverage of true values, not only average returns and std.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q3.1",
   "reviewer": "Q3",
   "text": "Benchmarks limited; no hard (Humanoid, Dog) or sparse-reward environments.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q3.2",
   "reviewer": "Q3",
   "text": "Missing modern exploration-focused baselines such as BRO.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q3.3",
   "reviewer": "Q3",
   "text": "Lambda sensitivity and exploration role insufficiently explored; contradictory results.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q4.1",
   "reviewer": "Q4",
   "text": "Continuous-time model-based RL with GP ODE models already studied (OCORL); incremental.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q4.2",
   "reviewer": "Q4",
   "text": "Figure 2 baselines only mean planner and PETS; need more SOTA comparisons.",
   "minor": false
  }
